# Client environment. Copy to `.env.local` for local overrides.
#
# IMPORTANT: Vite inlines VITE_* values at BUILD time, not at runtime. Changing
# any of these on the hosting platform requires a rebuild + redeploy — setting
# them on an existing deployment does nothing.

# ---- Local development ---------------------------------------
# Where `npm run dev` proxies /api and /socket.io. Read by vite.config.ts (a
# plain process.env, so it is NOT prefixed into the bundle).
# VITE_API_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8899

# ---- Production build ----------------------------------------
# Leave BOTH unset for a same-origin deploy (Express serving the built SPA):
# the client then uses relative /api/v1 and connects the socket to its own
# origin. Set them for the split deploy — the live one is the SPA on Vercel and
# the API on Railway, which is also why the server needs COOKIE_SAMESITE=none.
# VITE_API_BASE=https://swil-social-api-production.up.railway.app/api/v1
# VITE_SOCKET_URL=https://swil-social-api-production.up.railway.app

# ---- Monitoring (optional) -----------------------------------
# Unset means zero browser telemetry. Setting a DSN lazily loads @sentry/react.
# Web-vitals RUM posts to the app's own /api/v1/events regardless of this.
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
